## 6. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk                                                       | Severity | Likelihood | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **ChatApp constructor refactor breaks standalone mode**        | High     | Low        | `containerMode` defaults to `false`. All existing code paths unchanged when option not passed. Chatbot tests cover standalone behavior.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
| **Two DuckDB connections cause locking issues**                | Medium   | Very Low   | DuckDB supports multiple connections per instance. Both are read-only. `fromCache()` ensures single underlying instance.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
| **OPENROUTER_API_KEY missing in hub context**                  | High     | Medium     | Hub doesn't currently need this env var. The chatbot tab's `init()` should catch the error from `createModel()` and display a graceful message in the tab container ("Set OPENROUTER_API_KEY to use the chat").                                                                                                                                                        |
| **Chatbot deps increase hub bundle size**                      | Low      | Certain    | Deps are already in root `package.json`. Bun bundles tree-shakes unused code. The LangGraph/LangChain deps are only imported when the chatbot tab is created.                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| **Model selector overlay z-index conflicts with help overlay** | Medium   | Low        | Help overlay is in `workspaceBox` (line 164 of appShell.ts). Model selector overlay is on `renderer.root`. Root children render after workspaceBox children, so overlay appears on top. When help is visible and user presses `@`, the model selector should take precedence — this is handled by `ChatApp.handleKeyPress()` checking `modelSelector.overlay.visible` first. |
| **Escape key conflict: hub shutdown vs chatbot cancel**        | Medium   | Medium     | The adapter's `handleKeyPress()` checks `isProcessing`. When processing, Escape cancels the stream (chatbot behavior). When idle, Escape returns `false` so the hub's key router handles it (blur or shutdown).                                                                                                                                                          |
| **Tab `init()` failure blocks all tabs**                         | High     | Low        | `initTabs()` uses `Promise.all()` (appShell.ts:307). If chatbot init fails (e.g., no API key), ALL tabs fail. **Mitigation:** The chatbot tab's `init()` should catch errors and set an error state, displaying the error in its container rather than throwing.                                                                                                             |
| **CI fixture lacks chatbot-required tables**                   | Medium   | Medium     | Chatbot's `buildSystemPrompt()` queries `getTableRefs()` and `getColumns()`. The CI fixture (`data/fixtures/nba.ci.duckdb`) has a subset of tables. The system prompt builder should handle missing tables gracefully (it already does — it discovers what's available).                                                                                                   |
| **Strict chatbot typecheck breaks**                            | Low      | Low        | `tsconfig.chatbot.json` only includes `src/chatbot/**/*` and `src/shared/**/*`. The hub tab imports FROM chatbot but doesn't modify chatbot's type surface. No impact.                                                                                                                                                                                                   |

